    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (2/2). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the telephone-uniqueness rule for `POST /api/owners` (409 on a duplicate) with minimal structural impact \u2014 no existing Java method was modified. I added three small, cohesive units and one YAML wiring edit:\n\n- **`RejectDuplicateTelephone.java`** (new function, CC ~3): runs after `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, so the request telephone is already digits-only. It normalizes each stored owner's telephone the same way and throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match.\n- **`DuplicateTelephoneException.java`** (new checked exception, so it appears in the `throws` clause per the escalation contract).\n- **`DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java`** (new handler): responds `409 CONFLICT`.\n- **`...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`** (new escalation registration).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: inserted a `rejectDuplicateTelephone` step between `normalize` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance as the write steps.\n\nPlacing the check after normalization means comparison uses the canonical digits-only form, so `04...` vs `+61...`-style variants that normalize identically are correctly rejected. `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` confirms distinct telephones still succeed, and `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` confirms the 409.",
